<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23017" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-ĕquĭto</span></b> ,
			āre, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i>, <i>to ride upon</i>
			 or <i>over</i> any thing (post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, with <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sarmatae patentibus campis inequitant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor. 4, 12, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">horrenti fascino,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 4, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, with <i>acc.</i>:
			Aurora caelum inequitabat, <i>traversed the sky</i>,
			i. e. <i>the day broke</i>,
				<i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p. 129</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">id. ib. 6</span></i>, p. 177 <i>fin.</i>—And in mal. part.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestras matronas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 4, 131</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">medicina audet inequitare philosophiae,</span>”
				i. e. <i>to insult</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 7, 15, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frustra inequitas nobis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 7, p. 235</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
